From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:39:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] ci: add publishing workflows (images, PyPI, site) with
 configurable targets

- reusable-docker-release.yml: the v<version> and latest images of a released tool (api, federation-api, query-tool), built from the tool's folder with its Dockerfile (symlinks materialized in the build context), pushed to IMAGE_REGISTRY/IMAGE_NAMESPACE (repository variables), as upstream's build_docker_on_release.yml.
- reusable-docker-nightly.yml (api, federation-api) and reusable-docker-nightly-query-tool.yml (query-tool: amd64, version <version>-dev-<short sha>): the nightly images, as upstream's build_docker_nightly.yml; called by a `nightly` job in the tool's workflow on push to main after its tests pass.
- release.yml: for each tool released by release-please, its release image, reusable-configure-nb-release.yml (PyPI upload; PYPI_REPOSITORY_URL selects the index) and reusable-sites.yml.
- reusable-sites.yml: query-tool on Netlify, only when SITE_DEPLOY is true; also runnable by hand for a released version.
